// Workspace type-check config (Story 1.3 QA — closes the type-assertion gap).
//
// WHY THIS EXISTS:
//   The production build (`pnpm -r build` → per-package `tsc -b`) and the test
//   runner (`pnpm test` → Vitest/esbuild) BOTH skip type-checking the co-located
//   `*.test.ts` files:
//     - tsconfig.base.json `exclude`s `**/*.test.ts` from every package build, so
//       `tsc -b` never sees them.
//     - Vitest transforms via esbuild WITHOUT type-checking and has no `typecheck`
//       runner configured, so `expectTypeOf(...)` / `@ts-expect-error` in tests are
//       runtime NO-OPS — a deliberately wrong type assertion still passes.
//   Result: every type-level guarantee asserted in a test (e.g. EventPayloadMap
//   totality — that every EventType has a payload — which is enforced ONLY by the
//   compile-time `extends Record<EventType, object>` constraint, and the
//   `@ts-expect-error` closed-vocabulary / closed-error-code guards) was VACUOUS in
//   the default suite and in CI.
//
// WHAT THIS DOES:
//   A single, non-composite, `noEmit` pass that type-checks ALL workspace source
//   AND test files (it does NOT inherit the base `exclude`, so tests ARE checked).
//   Driven by the root `typecheck` script and wired as a hard CI gate, so the
//   test files' type assertions finally fail the run when they are wrong.
//
//   Kept as a SEPARATE config (not folded into the package builds) so the shipped
//   `dist` stays test-free and the "packages never redefine the root config"
//   convention is preserved — this is one root config, like vitest.config.ts.
//
// --- Cross-package `src` resolution via `paths` (Story 4.0, AC #1) ---
//   The `paths` block below maps each `@agentbbs/<pkg>` specifier to that package's
//   `src/index.ts` (live TypeScript SOURCE) — mirroring EXACTLY the Story 3.0 Vitest
//   `resolve.alias` in vitest.config.ts (same five package roots). Without it, this
//   single non-composite pass resolved cross-package specifiers through each package's
//   `exports` → built `dist/*.d.ts`, so a freshly-added cross-package `core` export
//   tripped `TS2307`/`TS2305` until `pnpm run build` was run first (the recurring
//   Epic 2/3 build-first papercut — deferred-work E3-typecheck-dist). With the mapping,
//   `pnpm run typecheck` resolves cross-package exports from `src` and no longer needs
//   a prior build. (Verified against the installed TS 6.0.3 from a no-`dist` state:
//   `--traceResolution` shows `@agentbbs/core` → `packages/core/src/index.ts`.)
//
//   NO `baseUrl` (intentional): the installed TypeScript is 6.0.3, where `baseUrl` is
//   DEPRECATED (`TS5101`, removed in TS 7.0). TS 4.1+ permits `paths` WITHOUT `baseUrl`
//   — the only constraint the 6.0 compiler enforces is that each path TARGET be
//   relative (a leading `./`, else `TS5090` "Non-relative paths are not allowed when
//   'baseUrl' is not set"); when `baseUrl` is omitted, targets resolve relative to THIS
//   config file's directory (the repo root), which is exactly what we want. So the
//   targets are written `./packages/<pkg>/src/index.ts`. This is future-proof past
//   TS 7.0 and avoids the deprecation diagnostic entirely (no `ignoreDeprecations`).
//
//   BUILD-MODE HONESTY: this `paths` block is TYPECHECK-CONFIG-ONLY by design — it
//   MUST NOT be added to tsconfig.base.json (which the per-package production builds
//   extend), or the shipped `dist` would resolve cross-package imports to source and
//   the build-honesty guard would be lost. `pnpm run build` (`pnpm -r build` →
//   per-package `tsc -b`) still compiles each package against the real `exports`/`dist`
//   and stays in the gate as the shipped-artifact guard, so this mapping does not mask
//   a broken barrel `exports`. Package ROOTS only (object key = exact specifier match);
//   no deep `@agentbbs/<pkg>/<subpath>` specifier is imported by any source/test
//   (grep-verified, as Story 3.0 confirmed for the Vitest alias).
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "composite": false,
    "declaration": false,
    "declarationMap": false,
    "sourceMap": false,
    // Node globals (`import.meta.url`, `node:*` builtins) are used by some test
    // files (e.g. the Story 1.2 boundary-enforcement test). Vitest's
    // expectTypeOf/assertType helpers resolve from the explicit `vitest` import,
    // so they need no ambient types entry here.
    "types": ["node"],
    // --- UI test tier (Story 9.1) ---
    // This single flat pass type-checks ALL workspace source+tests, INCLUDING the
    // ui-shared React/.tsx files (which the per-package tsconfig.json compiles with
    // its own `jsx`/`lib`, but this standalone config does NOT inherit). Without
    // these two options the .tsx here fail TS17004 (no --jsx) and TS2584 (no DOM
    // globals: document/getComputedStyle).
    //   - `jsx: react-jsx`: the React 19.2 automatic runtime; emits nothing under
    //     noEmit and is inert for the node packages (they contain no JSX).
    //   - DOM lib: needed for document/getComputedStyle/HTML*Element in the
    //     ui-shared DOM test. NOTE: this does NOT weaken the node packages'
    //     no-browser-globals guarantee — each node package's PRODUCTION build
    //     (`tsc -b` with the base lib ["ES2023"], no DOM) is the per-package guard
    //     that still fails if a node package touches `document`. `pnpm run build`
    //     stays in the gate, so accidental DOM use in a node package is caught
    //     there; only this aggregate typecheck pass sees DOM (deliberately, for the
    //     one presentation package). Widening `lib` (a global ambient) is preferred
    //     over widening `types` (which the story Task 5 cautioned against, as a
    //     `@types/*` entry would pull whole ambient package surfaces in).
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "lib": ["ES2023", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    // Resolve cross-package `@agentbbs/*` specifiers to each package's `src` barrel
    // (see header). No `baseUrl` (deprecated in TS 6.0); targets are RELATIVE to this
    // config's directory (repo root) and so must carry a leading `./`.
    "paths": {
      "@agentbbs/core": ["./packages/core/src/index.ts"],
      "@agentbbs/data-access": ["./packages/data-access/src/index.ts"],
      "@agentbbs/mcp-server": ["./packages/mcp-server/src/index.ts"],
      "@agentbbs/cli": ["./packages/cli/src/index.ts"],
      "@agentbbs/ui-shared": ["./packages/ui-shared/src/index.ts"]
    }
  },
  // Override the base `exclude` (which drops **/*.test.ts) so test files ARE
  // type-checked here. Only skip dependencies / build output.
  "exclude": ["**/node_modules/**", "**/dist/**"],
  "include": [
    "packages/*/src/**/*.ts",
    "packages/*/src/**/*.tsx",
    "apps/*/src/**/*.ts",
    "apps/*/src/**/*.tsx"
  ]
}
